{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nThe completion-verifier LLM runs even when the ticket's own Acceptance Criteria block still contains unchecked '- [ ]' items — a deterministic fail-fast condition. Backtest over verifier-passed closes found unchecked boxes only in [operator-attested]-shaped items (whose done-evidence legitimately lives outside the snapshot); non-attested unchecked boxes did not occur, so a precheck that exempts the attested tag adds no false rejections. check-ac exists but only as a readiness scorer, absent from the close path.\n\n## Approach\nIn the close transition path (before the LLM verifier dispatch), parse the ticket description's '## Acceptance Criteria' section; if any '- [ ]' checkbox remains unchecked, fail the close deterministically with a teaching message (check the box after satisfying it, or edit the AC with justification) — same style as existing DET short-circuits. EXEMPTION: a '- [ ]' line whose text after the checkbox begins with the case-insensitive '[operator-attested]' tag is NOT a violation — reuse the exact matcher (det_operator_attested._OPERATOR_ATTESTED_TAG_RE, src/rebar/llm/plan_review/det_operator_attested.py:44) rather than a parallel regex, so the two surfaces cannot drift. Exempt classes that skip the verifier today (duplicate/not_a_bug/escalated via replacement-link precheck) are untouched: the precheck runs only where the verifier would run.\n\n## Scope\n- src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py (precheck family, alongside _completion_precheck)\n- tests for the close path\n\n## Testing\nHappy: all boxes checked -> close proceeds to verifier. Unchecked box -> exit non-zero pre-LLM with the teaching message. Unchecked '- [ ] [operator-attested] ...' item -> precheck passes (exemption row, both lowercase and mixed-case tag). Non-completion classes (duplicate etc.) bypass unchanged. Description without checkbox syntax -> precheck passes (prose AC remains legal).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Close on a ticket with any unchecked, non-[operator-attested] '- [ ]' AC item fails deterministically BEFORE any LLM call, with remediation guidance.\n- [ ] Unchecked items carrying the [operator-attested] tag (matched via det_operator_attested's shared regex) are exempt and do not block the close.\n- [ ] Prose-only AC (no checkboxes) and non-completion close classes are unaffected.\n- [ ] Backtest property preserved: historical verifier-passed closes (including attested-shaped ones) would all still pass.\n- [ ] Tests cover checked, unchecked, attested-exempt (case-insensitive), prose-only, and exempt-class paths.\n"}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785711074878097001,"uuid":"6c42c953-7c0c-46c3-85f6-69c7c23834d8"}